{"type": "user", "session_id": "0a161ae7-fb44-49ef-ba93-6251941e6d27", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "You are one reviewer of a round of a layout review of a finished printed circuit board. You did not design it, and you have no notes from whoever did. Work only from the files in this folder. You can read and search them, and fetch a published document at its address; you cannot run a command, render a view or write anything.\n\nFollow the \"Layout review\" section of docs/board-design-method.md, as written, for the board design in hardware/proof/review-proof/ (its project, schematic, layout and rules files, its layout-plan.md and its design-rules.md, and every record those name). The round's own fields are in round.json: its number, its kind, the commit judged, the commands the views were rendered with and the pre-order check's lines. The views the method names are rendered already: views/ (views/index.txt lists every image with its caption fields, and views/facts.txt gives every net's facts), placement/ (placement/index.txt and placement/measures.txt), and the pre-order check's report is check-report.txt. Open each image a verdict rests on and read the board coordinates from its caption. Where an item needs a view that is not among them, give it `cannot judge` and write in Why `needs <view>: <why the views rendered do not show it>`. For a rule-kind item whose figure rests on a published document, fetch it at the address the board's rules table gives, or find it from the manufacturer or publisher the row names, and judge the figure against it; a document you cannot fetch makes t\n[12618 characters omitted]"}}
